have all last 20 positions reachable, need represent every offset 0..19 from some? Let's compute convergence maybe ~? For A=19,B=20, after time ~? reachable positions are 1 + combinations of 19,20. The last 20 positions all reachable when all residues? Around Frobenius 19*20-19-20=341, so hitting time ~360 > B^2=400 bound okay. Could be near A*B - A - B + B =? For consecutive-ish. Maximum conductor for two largest A=B-1 is (B-1)(B)-... ~B^2-... less B^2. With more moves semigroup can only improve. Bound B^2 likely safe. But mask full means last B positions all reachable including positions maybe not exactly all generated? Since reachable positions after time t are subset; full at time t requires all offsets 0..B-1 from current, i.e., all positions cur-B+1..cur reachable. These are consecutive large positions past conductor, so yes by conductor all are reachable if at least one starting reachable. Conductor of semigroup generated by [A,B] <=? For A=1 it's 0. Worst for A=B-1, conductor = (B-1)B-(B-1)-B = B^2-3B+1? Let's compute: for coprime a,b Frobenius ab-a-b, conductor = ab-a-b+1. For a=B-1,b=B: a*b -a -b+1 = B(B-1)-(B-1)-B+1 = B^2-3B+2? Wait B^2-B-B+1-B+1 = B^2-3B+2. Then to have last B consecutive reachable from start maybe need max representable among them etc, time maybe conductor+B ~ B^2-2B+2 < B^2. So LIMIT B^2 enough.\n\nBut nuance: Starting mask may have reachable positions not just a single position and could be near current. The earliest reachable position could be cur-B (distance B-1), then future moves from that position are shifted? The set of reachable offsets relative to current may not include 0? For mask nonzero, there is some p within last B reachable. From p, future positions p+s. To fill last B positions of cur after t steps, need for each offset q in [0,B-1], p+s = cur+q for some s in semigroup. Equiv s = (cur-p)+q. cur-p ≤ B-1. So need all numbers in [D,D+B-1] representable where D=cur-p ≤ B-1. Conductor C ~ B^2-3B+2. Then max of those D+B-1 =