B^2-2B+1. For A=B-1, B=20 => 361. B^2+5=405 enough. Good. With p0 maybe start not at cumulative? But at most B-1 offset, still bound B^2 maybe. Fine.\n\nLet's empirically check for all A<B<=20 the maximum convergence time from all nonzero masks? We can maybe just simulate starting from mask=1 for each pair (not all masks) to see max, since initial only mask=1 at very beginning, but after a bad segment reachable mask could be some arbitrary subset, potentially slower than starting from contiguous? Any nonzero mask contains some reachable position p with D=cur-p; from that p it is as if started earlier, so convergence time ≤ starting from single bit? Other bits only help. So worst initial mask is single bit, and by translation it's mask with a single bit at some position j. Need max over j for each A,B. Let's simulate all j for B<=20 to verify max hitting time <=B^2. Do inline."}
{"type": "tool_call", "callId": "call_00_wX2oFMq7itcRkJtKMK801447", "tool": "bash", "input": {"command": "cd /Users/b612-lp/bench-workspaces/r1030/dsh/lcb-recent-hard-4 && python3 - << 'PY'\nmx=0; arg=None\nfor B in range(2,21):\n    full=(1<<B)-1\n    for A in range(1,B):\n        allowed=((1<<(B-A+1))-1)<<(A-1)\n        for j in range(B):\n            mask=1<<j\n            t=0\n            while mask!=full and mask!=0 and t<=B*B+100:\n                nb=1 if (mask&allowed) else 0\n                mask=((mask<<1)|nb)&full\n                t+=1\n            if mask!=full:\n                print('not full',A,B,j,t,mask); raise SystemExit\n            if t>mx: mx=t; arg=(A,B,j)\nprint('max',mx,arg)\nPY", "description": "Check convergence bound for abc388_f", "timeoutMs": 120000}}
